# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Until these are set the app runs on the stub
# repository: real structure, no data.
#
# On Netlify these two live in the project's environment variables, not in a file —
# see "Connecting Supabase" in README.md. The VITE_ prefix is load-bearing: Vite only
# exposes prefixed variables to client code, and it inlines them into the bundle that
# ships to the browser.
#
# The Netlify Supabase extension writes the same two values under names of its own —
# VITE_SUPABASE_DATABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY. Both spellings are read, and the
# two below win when both are set. Locally, use these two.
#
# The key is the publishable one (`sb_publishable_…`) from Supabase's API settings.
# Never put the service role key here or anywhere else with a VITE_ prefix — it
# bypasses RLS, and a VITE_ variable is public the moment it is built.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
